{"title":"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution（spoken_in_Chinese）subtitle_in_English\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution（spoken in Chinese）subtitle in English</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Torus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the surface produced by revolving a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> around an axis in the plane of the circle that is a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from the center of the circle (so like a donut). Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a sphere with a radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> rests on the inside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, it is internally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> along a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c42077f2a447ca548cdbfe63f1932e9866df3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> rests on the outside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, it is externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> along a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/55687fca3ca459d307e26649477bacfaea5c0557.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />. The difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c78ad3426a3d3b0ebce44afc89cca26cabaf3aef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i-r_o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37022762ff3d1bc2d13275734410d4013b5e508.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by Mathemagician108 */ unitsize(0.3 inch); draw(ellipse((0,0), 3, 1.75)); draw((-1.2,0.1)..(-0.8,-0.03)..(-0.4,-0.11)..(0,-0.15)..(0.4,-0.11)..(0.8,-0.03)..(1.2,0.1)); draw((-1,0.04)..(-0.5,0.12)..(0,0.16)..(0.5,0.12)..(1,0.04)); draw((0,2.4)--(0,-0.15)); draw((0,-0.15)--(0,-1.75), dashed); draw((0,-1.75)--(0,-2.25)); draw(ellipse((2,0), 1, 0.9)); draw((2.03,-0.02)--(2.9,-0.4)); [/asy]\" width=\"218\" height=\"168\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, let's consider a section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the solids, along the axis.\nBy some 3D-Geomerty thinking, we can simply know that the axis crosses the sphere center. So, that is saying, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> we took crosses one of the equator of the sphere.\n</p><p>Here I drew two graphs, the first one is the case when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is internally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d1bcb73ba68266bd9d518d4246fe3974b37fef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.35cm); pair O = (0, 0); real r1 = 11; real r2 = 3; draw(circle(O, r1)); pair A = O + (0, -r1); pair B = O + (0, r1); draw(A--B); pair C = O + (0, -1.25*r1); pair D = O + (0, 1.25*r1); draw(C--D, dashed); dot(O); pair E = (2 * r2, -sqrt((r1 - r2) * (r1 - r2) - 4 * r2 * r2)); pair F = (0, -sqrt((r1 - r2) * (r1 - r2) - 4 * r2 * r2)); pair G = (-r2 * O + r1 * E) / (r1 - r2); pair H = (-r2 * O + r1 * F) / (r1 - r2); draw(circle(E, r2)); draw(circle((-2 * r2, -sqrt((r1 - r2) * (r1 - r2) - 4 * r2 * r2)), r2)); draw(O--G, dashed); draw(F--E, dashed); draw(G--H, dashed); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, SW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW); label(&quot;$E_i$&quot;, E, NE); label(&quot;$F_i$&quot;, F, W); label(&quot;$G_i$&quot;, G, SE); label(&quot;$H_i$&quot;, H, W); label(&quot;$r_i$&quot;, 0.5 * H + 0.5 * G, NE); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, 0.5 * E + 0.5 * G, NE); label(&quot;$11$&quot;, 0.5 * O + 0.5 * G, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"365\" height=\"458\" />\n</p><p>and the second one is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fb5d4d1ae5297959727a179a10ed94e72e66dc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.35cm); pair O = (0, 0); real r1 = 11; real r2 = 3; draw(circle(O, r1)); pair A = O + (0, -r1); pair B = O + (0, r1); draw(A--B); pair C = O + (0, -1.25*(r1 + r2)); pair D = O + (0, 1.25*r1); draw(C--D, dashed); dot(O); pair E = (2 * r2, -sqrt((r1 + r2) * (r1 + r2) - 4 * r2 * r2)); pair F = (0, -sqrt((r1 + r2) * (r1 + r2) - 4 * r2 * r2)); pair G = (r2 * O + r1 * E) / (r1 + r2); pair H = (r2 * O + r1 * F) / (r1 + r2); draw(circle(E, r2)); draw(circle((-2 * r2, -sqrt((r1 + r2) * (r1 + r2) - 4 * r2 * r2)), r2)); draw(O--E, dashed); draw(F--E, dashed); draw(G--H, dashed); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, SW); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, NW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NW); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, SW); label(&quot;$E_o$&quot;, E, NE); label(&quot;$F_o$&quot;, F, SW); label(&quot;$G_o$&quot;, G, S); label(&quot;$H_o$&quot;, H, W); label(&quot;$r_o$&quot;, 0.5 * H + 0.5 * G, NE); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, 0.5 * E + 0.5 * G, NE); label(&quot;$11$&quot;, 0.5 * O + 0.5 * G, NE); [/asy]\" width=\"365\" height=\"518\" />\n</p><p>For both graphs, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of sphere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are the intersections of the sphere and the axis. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (ignoring the subscripts) is one of the circle centers of the intersection of torus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (again, ignoring the subscripts) is one of the tangents between the torus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and sphere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> on section <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9418b3ef3cb0ca9d7b7726f48167a4d248d66f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF\\bot CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/49685d4d11bb28b78746f6eddae7b1840da300a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG\\bot CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>And then, we can start our calculation.\n</p><p>In both cases, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fe2aebbeed36e9be5e2d0d465a828a4bedfaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta OEF\\sim \\Delta OGH\\Longrightarrow \\frac{EF}{OE} =\\frac{GH}{OG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"276\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Hence, in the case of internal tangent, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1be698cb13b9a7aaf682689044bbc3d69d77e9f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{E_iF_i}{OE_i} =\\frac{G_iH_i}{OG_i}\\Longrightarrow \\frac{6}{11-3} =\\frac{r_i}{11}\\Longrightarrow r_i=\\frac{33}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"349\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>In the case of external tangent, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c3f1128efeb3612b9484971e58c620917d5893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{E_oF_o}{OE_o} =\\frac{G_oH_o}{OG_o}\\Longrightarrow \\frac{6}{11+3} =\\frac{r_o}{11}\\Longrightarrow r_o=\\frac{33}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"359\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Thereby, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cdd933973aa635a4483df27887f3e8685f21a5fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i-r_o=\\frac{33}{4}-\\frac{33}{7}=\\frac{99}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"191\" height=\"38\" />. And there goes the answer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7dd74d66732ad26d4a8e1609ec220c6fbc738b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99+28=\\boxed{\\mathbf{127} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"127\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Prof_Joker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_AIME_II_8.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3c/2024_AIME_II_8.png/230px-2024_AIME_II_8.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"230\" height=\"341\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/3c/2024_AIME_II_8.png/345px-2024_AIME_II_8.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/3c/2024_AIME_II_8.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/e/9de7919e7f349c0717c99f2da3ad9c13369696b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OC = OD = 11, AC = BD =  3, EC&#39; = FD&#39; = 6.\\]\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a59caa41d55560bb53b33a56d5e21a4072073c44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {CC&#39;}{C&#39;E} = \\frac{AC}{OA} \\implies CC&#39; = \\frac {3 \\cdot 6}{11-3}\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc57e0effc941fb00e00fa560ad44e99cf51d3b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {DD&#39;}{DB} = \\frac{FD&#39;}{OB} \\implies DD&#39; = \\frac {3 \\cdot 6}{11+3}\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbdddad9345e463423ed9c9fde580fcaf4a732e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[CC&#39; + DD&#39; = \\frac {9}{4}+\\frac {9}{7} = \\frac {99}{28}.\\]\" width=\"213\" height=\"37\" />\n<b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-1HLRjtLCSM\">https://youtu.be/-1HLRjtLCSM</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.EF.BC.88spoken_in_Chinese.EF.BC.89subtitle_in_English\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution（spoken_in_Chinese）subtitle_in_English\">Video Solution（spoken in Chinese）subtitle in English</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution（spoken in Chinese）subtitle in English\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YdQdDBROG8U\">https://youtu.be/YdQdDBROG8U</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II\" title=\"2024 AIME II\">2024 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href